I've met a few other nethack players in the most unexpected of
places.  Heck, I work with another one (he's never ascended and plays
more than I do).  When ascension counts come up, I have yet to
randomly meet anyone with more than 3 ascension.  After sheepishly
admitting to having "over forty with a seven-game streak", I'm often
on the receiving end of dumbfounded looks and/or accused of lying.

So ... I'd say your typical hardcore nethacker has ascended, at most,
a few times.  The hardcore paranoid-android types (self included) who
reel off ascension streaks with clockwork regularity are statistical
outliers.  An rgrn regular probably has their perception skewed
because a significant chunk of the posting community consists of
serial ascenders.

For example, there are over 29,500 usernames on NAO.  1,126 of these
have ascended.  I am not attempting to control for the "one-player,
several accounts" silliness.  That way lies madness.  Stealing from
http://alt.org/nethack/ascstreak.html gives a picture of just how
unusual going back-to-back really is:

Longest Ascension Streak:
10 or more games (10 players)
9 games (2 players)
8 games (2 players)
7 games (5 players)
6 games (6 players)
5 games (13 players)
4 games (21 players)
3 games (53 players)
